47|0@NoStupidQuestions^1440340168#cuctenf:doc_daneeka$:Tea used to be the normal drink in the American colonies too, before the imposition of a special tax that eventually led to the Boston Tea Party. After that, it became a popular thing among patriots to drink coffee instead as a way of protesting the tax, and also the various other 'intolerable acts' the government imposed as punitive measures after the Tea Party.
20|0@NoStupidQuestions^1440345706#cucw01u:lorde_blue$:Tea used to be huge in the American colonies. It was a joke in England about how much Americans loved their tea. Let that sink in for a minute.
